#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""B3: Go-model interacting-bead stochastic dynamics on a reference configuration.

Model (reduced units, bead mass = 1, k_B = 1):
  backbone bonds : U = k_b (r - r0_i)^2,  k_b = 5.0, r0_i = reference bond length
  native contacts: U = 2*eps*((s/r)^12 - (s/r)^10), s = r0_ij (reference pair
                   distance); eps = 1/0.13395 so the well depth is exactly 1.0
  non-native     : U = 2*eps_nn*(s_nn/r)^12, eps_nn = 0.5, s_nn = 3.0, all pairs
                   |i-j| >= 2 that are not native contacts

Integrator: BAOAB Langevin split, gamma = friction, dt = dt_reduced:
  B: x += v dt/2 ; A: v <- exp(-g dt) v + sqrt(T (1 - exp(-2 g dt))) xi
  O: v += F dt ; A: (same OU) ; B: x += v dt/2

Order parameter (single deterministic criterion, used in EVERY Q-based output):
  Q(t) = (1/M) sum_{(i,j) in native} 1[ r_ij(t) <= 1.5 * r0_ij ]
"""
